{"title":"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Somewhat_Cheating)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Somewhat Cheating)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Triangle_Inequality_but_Easier_For_Those_Who_Know_Logs_Well)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Triangle Inequality but Easier For Those Who Know Logs Well)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For how many integral values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can a triangle of positive area be formed having side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5c32e99d62f9862741ea8e4b5504604f26156a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{2} x, \\log_{4} x, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"19\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/529ec07cc85781dfd16ae43a56c75b109142bcfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 57 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 59 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 61 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 62 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 63$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For these lengths to form a triangle of positive area, the Triangle Inequality tells us that we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/8/53816532ec0773f5ef34eaf982b0b4ec12f1b524.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_2{x} + \\log_4{x} &gt; 3\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4b5db6cd5a9d33ce2efd052cc2ef64145c7808a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_2{x} + 3 &gt; \\log_4{x}\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e419e588cbc0f1b20fda03fc9bca2372d54084f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_4{x} + 3 &gt; \\log_2{x}.\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"17\" /> The second inequality is redundant, as it's always less restrictive than the last inequality. \n</p><p>Let's raise the first inequality to the power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/1/f91d0ef3148951abb921a3cf296c47277ac08fea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^{\\log_2{x}} \\cdot 4^{\\log_4{x}} &gt; 64 \\Rightarrow \\left(2^2\\right)^{\\log_2{x}} \\cdot x &gt; 64 \\Rightarrow x^2 \\cdot x &gt; 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"415\" height=\"25\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/5/af505a7aebbcf901ae1ededba228f8acc738b337.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Doing the same for the third inequality gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97d0bb85cedbbcf216463104f09d9f7c542c8adc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^{\\log_4{x}} \\cdot 64 &gt; 4^{\\log_2{x}} \\Rightarrow 64x &gt; x^2 \\Rightarrow x &lt; 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"322\" height=\"16\" /> (where we are allowed to divide both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be positive in order for the logarithms given in the problem statement to even have real values).\n</p><p>Combining our results, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer strictly between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />, so the number of possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/a/a8aff79b1e0b71ea41ecd3d7c69554c22c70f816.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64 - 4 - 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 59}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"171\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~Minor edits by BakedPotato66\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Somewhat_Cheating.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Somewhat_Cheating)\">Solution 2 (Somewhat Cheating)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Somewhat Cheating)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the triangle inequality, you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/52966876e0afbe490a7e77396f5ab0621a606841.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2{x}+\\log_4{x} &gt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"17\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/5/af505a7aebbcf901ae1ededba228f8acc738b337.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />. Now we need an upper-bound for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and since we're dealing with bases of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we're looking for answer choices close to a power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. All the answer choices seem to be around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />, and plugging that into the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50d8a94b639b3d50740dba956f24dc7b7b0cd03b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+\\log_4{x} &gt; \\log_2{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"17\" /> we see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> is the correct number. Now we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/7/b67125eac53f08765740a5f026f6f9689f1c4a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64 &gt; x &gt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> and the number of integers in between is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81a7a9525b9b64378a0097e6b6fba14368c1f348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64-4-1 = \\boxed{{59 \\textbf{(B)}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"163\" height=\"28\" /> --OGBooger\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Triangle_Inequality_but_Easier_For_Those_Who_Know_Logs_Well.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Triangle_Inequality_but_Easier_For_Those_Who_Know_Logs_Well)\">Solution 3 (Triangle Inequality but Easier For Those Who Know Logs Well)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Triangle Inequality but Easier For Those Who Know Logs Well)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can rewrite  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/9/b49a6fb9b78c4c85b28b5def651d2c644fc0c99c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_4{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/c/6dc8780a5d5b83a2f51dc57ef7f9b32a8287eb77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\log_2{x}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"39\" />. Now, we can just make our 3 equations:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e773d0d6f2c91beccad9f03125d7426314fc2749.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_2{x} + 3 &gt; \\frac{\\log_2{x}}{2}\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e99882c14adcf8ca3892789dcf1b69f413a047b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\log_2{x}}{2}+ 3 &gt; \\log_2{x}.\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/f/5fffdc5260accd2185ae532d23cc7a672e571066.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_2{x} + \\frac{\\log_2{x}}{2}&gt; 3\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"37\" />, from which we can quickly find an open upper and lower bound for x of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />, and the total number of integers in the range that satisfy is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81a7a9525b9b64378a0097e6b6fba14368c1f348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64-4-1 = \\boxed{{59 \\textbf{(B)}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"163\" height=\"28\" /> -- AncientKarnivore\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B\">2019 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017021921\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 290/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2296/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 156/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7141/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.801      1 -total\n 56.79%    8.406      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 41.69%    6.171      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17319:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017021921 and revision id 293756. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}